10. Kehar Singh v. The State (Delhi Administration
) , it was held (para 117) :
"The compliance of the sub-sec. (2) of S. 164 is therefore, mandatory and imperative and non-compliance of it renders the confession inadmissible in evidence. Section 463 of the Criminal P.C. provides that where the questions and answers regarding the confession have not been recorded evidence can be adduced to prove that in fact the requirements of sub-section (2) of Section 164 read with S. 281 have been complied with.
